<Base lang="en" path="about" localized={false} title="About - HTML5 Advent" description="Who publishes HTML5 Advent, how its guides are written and corrected, and how the site is funded." schema={schema}>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About HTML5 Advent</h1>

    <p>HTML5 Advent publishes practical guides to the modern web platform: HTML, CSS, JavaScript
    and the browser APIs that sit between them. The aim is narrow on purpose — explain what a
    feature actually does, what it costs, and when not to use it.</p>

    <h2>Who writes this</h2>
    <p>The site is edited independently by a single editorial team. It is not operated on behalf of
    any browser vendor, framework or hosting company, and no article is commissioned or reviewed by
    a third party before publication.</p>

    <h2>How guides are written</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Specifications and documentation first.</strong> Behaviour is described from the
      published specification or the vendor's own documentation, not from what a framework's
      marketing page claims.</li>
      <li><strong>No invented numbers.</strong> No benchmarks we have not run, no ratings, no
      "trusted by" claims, no fabricated adoption figures. Where a figure comes from a third party,
      it is attributed and dated.</li>
      <li><strong>Dated and corrected.</strong> Web platform behaviour moves. Guides carry a
      publication date and are corrected when a browser changes what they describe — corrections
      are made in place rather than quietly deleted.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How this site is funded</h2>
    <p>Some guides contain affiliate links, mainly to hosting and developer tools. If you follow one
    and subscribe, we may receive a commission at no extra cost to you. These links are disclosed on
    every page that carries one, and they never change which tool a guide recommends: the
    recommendation is decided before any offer is attached to it.</p>

    <h2>Corrections and contact</h2>
    <p>If a guide is wrong, out of date, or unclear, tell us — that is the fastest way for it to
    improve. Write to <a href="mailto:referencement.frb@gmail.com">referencement.frb@gmail.com</a>,
    or see the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. How we handle analytics and data is set out on
    the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
